Task: "crumpled barcode fails to read." Engineering — 3 days.

Step-by-step breakdown:
waiting for analytics — 4 days;
writing requirements — 1 day;
waiting for design — 5 days (designer shared with another product);
engineering — 3 days;
waiting for code review — 2 days;
waiting for testing — 4 days;
waiting for release window (releases on Thursdays) — 3 days.

Work — 4 days, waiting — 18. Speeding up engineering is pointless.

What was done: capped work in progress at six tasks, involved designer earlier during requirements, moved to on-demand releases. Cycle time dropped from 22 days to 9 without adding a single person.
